<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 77,136 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 77,136 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-09-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 77,136 tonnes of export and import cargo in 24 hours to 7.00 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Sunday, compared to 32,995 tonnes in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					   Sunday	    Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			 5,634	   15,059</p>
<p>    Import cargo			17,936	   71,502</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, four ships sailed and five berthed. In the next 24 hours, two ships were expected to sail and six were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		  Berthing</p>
<p>Vegoil		   10,800	 Tiblisi	     20/9</p>
<p>Crude oil		61,000	 Capitan Mirinda   21/9</p>
<p>High speed deisel    56,000	 Keefan		21/9</p>
<p>Palm oil		 13,000	 Bunga Angarik     23/9</p>
<p>Motor gasoline	 26,200	 Iter		  22/9</p>
<p>Gas oil		  40,000	 Santa Lucia	 31/9</p>
<p>Palm oil		  8,000	 Strength	    21/9</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
